<title>NETHERLANDS: Lanschot raises EPS forecast Hoogovens.</title>
<headline>Lanschot raises EPS forecast Hoogovens.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of March 6 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------------Price---Broker--------</p>
<p>Hoogovens	 Basic industries    91.00   Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: OUTPERFORMER (Reiterated). The outlook for Hoogovens net income in 1997 and 1998 has clearly improved. Aluminum prices have improved 15 pct in 1997 so far, and 50 pct in the last half year. The companies firm stance towards unions in both Belgium (considering 50 pct stake in Gustave Boel) and the Netherlands (considering lay off of 3.000 employees) and the improved outlook for the steel division, because of higher expected investments, are reasons for expected improvement.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     pvs EPS   P/E    P/CF   Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     9.67		  9.4    3.4    3.00</p>
<p>    1997		 12.50    (11.00)   7.3    3.2    3.00</p>
<p>    1998		 17.00    (15.50)   5.4    2.7    4.00</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
